    "Every truth is non-null in this file, so N equals the line count.",
    "'first' row = largest tau satisfying the condition; tau <= 120 is applied to the row's tau (so 120.25 is excluded, 119.25 is the first eligible second).",
    "LOCKED at T-120 uses fixed['120'].st in {LOCKED, PROVEN LOCKED}; fixed['120'].gate is ignored.",
    "continuous: count of LOCKED/PROVEN LOCKED rows after q (tau < q.tau) with side == q.side >= round(q.tau - 0.25), and not warned, not dirChange. q.tau - 0.25 is always integral so rounding mode is moot.",
    "created_time parsed to ms by truncating (not rounding) the fraction to 3 digits; short fractions are right-padded.",
    "'within 10 s before' = 0 <= signal ts - print ms <= 10000 (the strict < 10000 count is also reported). Percentiles in item 7 are over the signals that have such a print; percentiles over any prior print are given as a sensitivity.",
